atarashii asa ni deau toki ga ugakidasuyo

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.300
Maybe her memory has returned...

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.600
Maybe she remembered about herself and returned home.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.720
Yeah...

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.730
Maybe she did.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:30.940
Going somewhere?

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:32.440
Oh, yeah.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.940
I'll leave the door unlocked.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:41.280
<b>The Girls' Opinion</b>

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.590
Manga Cafe

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.190
Makoto!

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.580
Sorry.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:12.900
Manga Cafe
Sorry.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.730
Manga Cafe

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.650
Where in the world did she go?
Manga Cafe

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.550
Manga Cafe

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.070
She doesn't have anywhere to go home...

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.200
Makoto...?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.710
What the hell, geez!

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.870
She made us worry.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:41.840
Give me two Nikuman, please.
(TL Note: Nikuman = Pork Bun)

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.430
Now what?

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.350
She doesn't have enough money?

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.560
Oh damn!

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.480
What am I doing?

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.420
This sure is a long climb.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.510
Where is she going to?

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.220
Is her house located in a place like this?

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.080
Come here.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:56.380
It's going to be half and half.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.800
We're the same.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.880
We don't have anywhere to go...

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:08.060
"When he's taken in, he might be truly happy for a while,"

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.640
"but he's going to be far more miserable when he's eventually abandoned again."

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.520
I'm tired.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:18.190
It was hard for me to find you.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.440
Well, let's sleep...

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.530
I'm so sleepy right now...

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:25.490
We'd like to sleep in a warm futon, right?

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.130
You're an idiot.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.840
You're gonna catch a cold if you sleep here.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.840
Here, we're going home.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.890
You want to come too?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.000
Are you awake?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.880
Um, why am I here?

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:24.090
Yuuichi-san brought you here.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.130
Where's my cat!?

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.430
Good morning.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.430
Nayuki, we're gonna be late if you're going to watch the cat forever.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.480
Yeah, I'll come now.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.230
I'll be leaving.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:44.070
Idiot, the people remaining in the house say "Come back safely".

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:46.740
I can stay here?

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.360
Of course.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:50.660
That kitty too?

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:54.490
Accepted.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.620
Okay, then I'll be leaving.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.380
Wait, Yuuichi!

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.710
Yeah, come back safely.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.300
That was a relief.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:10.430
Yeah, sorry Nayuki.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.850
You're allergic to cats...

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.510
It's alright. I like cats.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.890
Hey, would you look for me if I ran away from home?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.020
You!

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:22.610
Stop saying stupid things. Let's go.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:26.690
What is it?

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.990
It's a notice about the ball.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.950
Huh? Ball?

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.870
It's an annual event every year.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.120
I don't take part in it though.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.500
Isn't it something that everyone takes part in?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.580
It's an event that the student council runs.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.500
It's not right for someone like me to go.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:45.170
That's why.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:47.880
Plaster Bust Sketching

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.300
Huh? Where's Yuuichi?

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.010
He went to buy bread.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.520
I have bread...

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.150
Perhaps he went to buy some to eat?

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:09.320
I'm sleepy.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:16.870
Sorry.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.330
Thank you very much!

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:22.460
You're having fun.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.380
I hate someone who says that.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.340
Why don't we go in first?

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.550
In the school building?

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:32.840
But I...

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.340
It's alright.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:36.390
It's okay?

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:40.100
Yeah, I can't let someone with a cold stay outside.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:44.190
Do you have a cold?

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.690
Yeah... I stayed out last night.

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:49.480
Take care of yourself.

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:52.240
If Shiori said that, then I have to take care of myself.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:54.610
What is it?

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.240
It seems to be practice for the ball.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:58.990
You know about it?

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.000
Yes, it's my dream.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.620
Since that time I saw my sister wear a dress to the ball, I began thinking...

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.170
"Oh, I would like to wear a beautiful dress like that".

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:12.130
Shiori, do you have a sister?

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.970
Yes. Didn't I tell you?

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.510
Is she beautiful?

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:22.180
Yes! She has long wavy hair, a slender figure, and she's a genius!

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.060
What's her name?

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:25.730
Misaka Kaori.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:32.280
I said I don't have any sisters!

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:35.780
That girl, why did she say something like that?

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.450
Did something happen?

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:41.750
Um, then why don't you go to the ball?

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:43.790
I can't.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.290
Wearing a dress...

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.210
But with Yuuichi-san...

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:54.630
Aizawa, leave after you put your easel away!

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.010
Oh, sorry.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.890
Um, I'll be going now.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.430
Okay, see you.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.350
Huh? Who was that girl?

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.060
Kaori, that's your sister right?

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.190
What are you talking about?

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:07.810
Stop fooling me.

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:10.020
You have a cute sister like that.

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:11.820
You are mistaken!?

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:19.780
Hey, wait!

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.580
I have a club meeting right now.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:25.040
Can you stop delaying me?

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.580
What was she on about?

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.340
Yuuichi-san!

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:37.630
How about eating lunch together with us?

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.810
It looks delicious!

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.650
Help yourself. Please eat without reservation.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:55.690
Itadakimasu!

00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:59.660
Passed!

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.660
What is?

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:03.660
For my bride!

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:08.670
If you say something like that, then everyone will be Yuuichi-san's bride.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:12.170
Kaori should be friendly like this.

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:17.470
There's an unfriendly person here too.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:21.140
Mai has been like this from the start.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:22.550
"From the start"?

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:23.930
Yes.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:28.480
Even I rarely see her smiling.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:29.980
That's not good!

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:32.020
Something like that is not good.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:35.360
You need to have a bright image change!

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:42.950
You always look mad so you get the label that says, "A delinquent girl who comes to school at night and breaks windows."

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:44.660
Mai! Try to smile!

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.080
Brighter!

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:52.670
She looks scary.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:55.710
It's no good.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.380
She has to change fundamentally.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.680
Oh yeah! This!

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:06.890
She should be in the ball!

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:11.980
If you dress up in a beautiful dress and dance elegantly, Mai will be a popular person!

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.980
No one will call you a delinquent anymore!

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:16.690
That's impossible, Yuuichi-san.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:18.230
Why?

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:21.200
It's a good chance to give Mai an "image up"!

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:27.160
No, Mai and I don't have dresses for the ball.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:28.410
Seriously?

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.330
Yes. We're just ordinary girls.

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.210
Oh man.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:37.500
I can hear the sound of my "Kawasumi Mai, Popular Person Project" shattering...

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.760
Stop with that "Something Project".

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:42.880
But...

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.180
If Yuuichi-san is thinking about Mai that much...

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:53.270
Okay, I'll ask someone I know.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.230
I didn't even "ask" you to do anything.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:56.980
Please do it!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.980
Is a tuxedo alright for you, Yuuichi-san?

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:02.700
I'm going to take part as well?

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.490
You're not?

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:06.570
You will, right?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:20.410
Tama!
(TL Note: Tama = Turtle)

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:21.830
Mayuge.
(TL Note: Mayuge = Eyebrows)

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:22.240
(TL Note: Mayuge = Eyebrows)

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:23.330
Why Mayuge?
(TL Note: Mayuge = Eyebrows)

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.290
Well, I just felt like it.

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:26.960
Then, Mikke!

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:28.540
Hanage.
(TL Note: Hanage = Nose Hair)

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:30.670
Get your head away from "hair"!

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:33.300
Have you decided? On the cat's name?

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:35.800
Yes! It's going to be Akahige!
(TL Note: Akahige = Red Mustache)

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:38.890
How about Taiyaki?

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:40.470
That kind of name...

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:42.430
And hey, where did you come from!?

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:45.060
When I was shopping, I met her by coincidence.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:46.730
Again?

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:49.440
Since you're here, how about having dinner with us?

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:50.610
Yes!

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.270
You should be more reserved.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:56.400
But, maybe the name of a food can be cute and suitable.

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:57.570
Like what?

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:00.070
Like Ichigo or Choco.
(T/L Note: Ichigo = strawberry, choco = chocolate)

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:01.870
Like Nikuman or Anman.
(TL Note: Nikuman = Pork Bun, Anman = Bean Paste Bun)

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:03.160
Whaaaaat!?

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.370
No? Then...

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.830
How about Piroshki?

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.500
That is...

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:11.170
Sawatori Piroshki!

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:12.750
Piro for short!

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:14.460
How about it? Isn't it cute?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.380
Hmmm... Piro...

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:20.180
See, he says he likes it!

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.180
I choose it!

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:24.850
From today, you're Piro!

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:27.310
Hey, what's a Piroschki?

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:27.850
Piro!
Hey, what's a Piroschki?

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:28.060
Piro!

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:28.270
It's a Russian meat-filled fried bread.

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:29.140
Hey Piro!
It's a Russian meat-filled fried bread.

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:29.690
It's a Russian meat-filled fried bread.

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:30.900
It's a good name, isn't it?
It's a Russian meat-filled fried bread.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:31.310
It's a good name, isn't it?

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:31.690
Maybe... Is it something like a Nikuman?

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:32.400
Piro!
Maybe... Is it something like a Nikuman?

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:32.440
Maybe... Is it something like a Nikuman?

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:33.310
Piro!
Maybe... Is it something like a Nikuman?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.070
Maybe... Is it something like a Nikuman?

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:34.480
She likes it so it's fine!

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:36.820
Do you like it? Hey, Piro!
She likes it so it's fine!

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:38.740
Is it "fine" as you say?

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:44.080
What's wrong?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.410
It's alright. I just felt giddy.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.000
Should I help you?

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:49.080
It's alright.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:51.250
I'll help you too!

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:52.960
You can do it?

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.630
Leave it to me!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:00.760
Ughuu...

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:03.010
Um, Ayu-chan...

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:04.850
We're okay over here.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:08.020
I think you should call home to say that you're going to be back late.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.730
Hey, hey! Let's read manga together!

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.440
Read it by yourself.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.940
Hey, hey! Let's make paper airplanes together!

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:18.650
Make them by yourself.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:20.070
Hey, hey!

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.240
You're boisterous!

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:23.700
Can't get an answer?

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:26.240
Did I dial it wrong?

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.790
Maybe they went shopping.

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:37.800
Maybe they left you to go eat something good!

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:41.470
Yuuichi!

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:43.380
It's just a joke.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.970
If it's fine by you, Ayu-chan, you can stay here overnight.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:48.350
That's a good idea!

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:51.230
We can put the futon in my room!

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.830
Huh? You're going somewhere?

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.080
Yeah.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:18.590
Is it a good time for you right now?

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:20.800
It's okay, but where's Nayuki?

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:23.970
She fell asleep as soon as she laid down on the futon.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.340
That's incredible!

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:26.890
I see.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:29.640
Akiko-san and Nayuki-san are both kind people, aren't they?

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.310
What's this about all of a sudden?

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:38.190
I am so happy because it has been a while since I had dinner in a merry atmosphere.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.650
I see.

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:44.360
Hey, do you remember the things from seven years ago?

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:50.830
When I was separated from my mom, you gave me some when I was crying...

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:52.200
The taiyaki...

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:57.580
It was so warm and sweet and delicious!

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:00.920
You really remember the taste from 7 years ago?

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:02.840
Of course I remember!

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.840
I was very happy!

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:06.630
But...

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:08.550
What's wrong?

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.300
I remember something too!

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:13.100
About the hand-made cookies you gave me!

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:19.360
It was soooo black like gravel.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.190
It wasn't something I could eat.

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:25.320
Ughuuu... You're mean.

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:26.360
It's the truth.

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:29.950
Yuuichi-kun really hasn't changed from the past.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.620
Like the cantankerous bit.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:34.410
You think so?

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.620
You haven't changed.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:39.210
You're the Yuuichi-kun that I liked.

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:45.260
The "like" I said is not that "like", but...

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:45.380
Don't panic...

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.470
Ah, what'd I say...
Don't panic...

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:47.130
Ah, what'd I say...

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:49.930
It's a serious problem! Piro is...

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:55.470
He's shivering all the time.

00:17:55.730 --> 00:17:58.770
And I thought maybe he was cold, so I put him in the futon...

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:00.770
This must be a cold.

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:01.650
Cold?

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.650
Makoto, heat some water!

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:05.400
We're going to warm him with a hot water bottle.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:06.190
Yeah!

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:09.410
Also, put a towel in a cardboard box and put him in there.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.950
It's best to leave him alone for now.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:13.330
I got it!

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:15.910
You're used to this, Yuuichi-kun.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:19.040
When I was a kid, I had a pet.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:20.750
What did you have?

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:28.880
Huh? I'm sure that I had a pet, but...

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:30.890
What was it...?

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:39.190
Mornin'. You're early today.

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:41.190
We have morning practice!

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:44.270
My jersey's not dry!

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:45.690
Are you alright?

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:47.780
I'm not alright!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:49.860
Huh? Where's Akiko-san?

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.570
It seems she's still sleeping.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.160
I'm leaving!

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:55.580
What's wrong with Akiko-san?

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:07.630
Akiko-san.

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:09.170
I'm sorry...

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:10.340
Breakfast...

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:12.180
Akiko-san!

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:14.050
You have a high fever!

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:16.680
It's alright. It's just a cold.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:18.890
You need to be lying down right now!

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:22.600
Ayu?

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:23.560
I don't want...

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:25.110
I... don't want...

00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:33.280
I don't want any sadness...

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:36.120
I don't want anyone else to disappear.

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:37.080
Idiot!

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:39.040
Akiko-san won't disappear!

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.040
Calm down, it's alright.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:43.540
Yeah...

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:56.800
Yuuichi-kun, go to school.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:57.350
Ayu?

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.600
I'll nurse Akiko-san, so...

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:01.890
Please.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:05.270
You won't listen to me even if I try to stop you, right?

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:10.030
I got it, I'll call you from school, so take care of Akiko-san.

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:16.160
Eh!? My mom is!?

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:18.160
It seems to be a cold.

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:19.370
There's no need to worry.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:24.790
It looks like her fever has gone down a bit.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:29.800
But, the medicine needs to be taken after a meal, so... um...

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:33.170
You'll have to make lunch...

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:38.720
But, her cooking is...

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.770
Right now, we need to believe in Ayu-chan!

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:44.890
Listen, I'm going to tell you how to make it.

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:46.020
Yeah...

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:48.270
First cut the ingredients into fine pieces.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:53.940
"Once it's boiling gently, remove the heat and add the egg!"

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:08.830
I'm home!

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:10.040
Welcome home!

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:11.630
How's Akiko-san?

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:15.590
Mom!

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:18.140
Are you okay now?

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:20.260
Yes, thanks to her.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.850
She nursed me the entire time.

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:30.610
I also worked hard nursing Piro!

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.610
Yup, you bet!

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:35.610
Mom...

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:37.820
Thank you, Ayu-chan.

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:00.890
Now it's fine!

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:30.170
